# Vacuum panel

A full `vacuum` tile is an edge-to-edge page: every `vacuum.*` in a list on the left, and start / pause / dock / locate plus fan speeds of the chosen one on the right (`vacuumCard`).

## Wiring

- Catalogue `vacuum.yaml`: sizes include `full`.
- Other tiles: `PANELS` entry `{ name: 'Vacuum panel', icon: 'robot-vacuum', domain: 'vacuum' }` — first vacuum entity, `full: true`.
- `Tile.edgeToEdge()` and `Tiles.kt` dispatch full vacuum to `vacuumPanel`. `hasOwnTaps` includes `vacuum`.
- UI state: `VacuumUiStore` / `RenderData.vacuumUi`. Verb `vacuum_select` → Rebuild.
- Selection: tile's entity, else the only vacuum, else the last `vacuum_select`. Controls reuse `vacuumCard` catalogue verbs on `e:<entity>`.

## Editor

`GridMockup.vue` draws list + Start/Pause/Dock/Locate. `TileDrawer.vue` treats full vacuum as edge-to-edge.

## Verify

